00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:11.501
Thank you so much!
Thank you so much!

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:14.267
That is -- Ouch!

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:15.701
-It is time.

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:17.000
We're hanging out with
Martin Short.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.834
It is time for "Short Stories
with Martin Short."

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:22.167
-♪ "Short Stories with

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.167
♪ Martin Short" ♪

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.901
-We're going to take
turns hitting this button here,

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:27.400
which is gonna generate
a random topic.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.167
We'll each will tell a short
story from our lives

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.501
about that topic.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.300
Martin, since you're the guest,
you will go first.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.467
Go ahead and press the button.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.467
Let's see what topic
we will be discussing.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:38.834
[ Beeping ]

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:41.868
-Okay, do you have
a story about...

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.634
meeting your heroes?

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:50.033
-Yes. In 1979, I went to my --
the first Golden Globes,

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.367
first time I'd ever been
to an award show.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:56.067
I was 29.
And I was in a TV show.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.100
And I went over,

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.601
and there was
Al Pacino sitting there.

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.601
[ Gasps ] I went over there.
I went over there.

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:01.968
And I was in a tux.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:04.934
And I went, "Mr. Pacino, I
just -- My name is Martin Short.

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:09.267
I just want to say to you that
you are the pinnacle to actors.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:13.267
You are the greatest genius and
you are an inspiration."

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.067
And he went, "Thanks.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.501
Um, I ordered a Stoli
about 10 minutes ago.

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:18.901
I'm wondering if you could --"

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:22.033
He thought I was the waiter.
He thought I was the waiter.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:26.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.667
-Okay.
You know what I'm going to do?

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.334
I'm going to
tell the story about --

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:34.067
I met you at a
"Saturday night Live"

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.300
after party.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.467
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:39.634
-Well, you're going --
You're going to win.

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.968
-I'm very competitive.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.901
But I remember meeting you
at an after party,

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:45.400
and I didn't know
what to say to you.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.634
I was so nervous.

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:47.767
And so, what I did was,

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:50.334
I just stared at you
from across the room

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:51.901
for the whole party.

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.000
And I just kept looking.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.133
And then you'd
look over or something.

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:56.033
And you were with Nancy,
your beautiful wife.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.968
And you just -- You looked over,
and I'd be like that or,

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:00.667
like [Chuckles]
"Hi," you know, or whatever.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.367
And then, eventually,
I think you just said --

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.834
-No, Nancy said, "Should we
invite the puppy dog over?"

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:06.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:08.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:10.067
-And she brought me over,
and I was like,

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.234
"I love you.

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:13.267
I love everything about you.
I love that."

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:15.767
I was doing lines from "I,
Martin Short, Goes Hollywood."

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.601
I was, like, reciting lines
from your bits.

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.534
-I remember that vividly.
-Alright, good. Okay, yeah.

00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:21.334
That was a time when you --
-That's a good one.

00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:22.868
-Next topic. Here we go.
-Do it.

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:25.434
[ Beeping ]

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:27.934
-I hope I have
a story about this.

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:29.100
-Oh!

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.367
-Now, I've never met you in
The White House,

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:31.367
so this won't be about you.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.167
-Yeah.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:36.267
I met George W. Bush
the first time

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:37.467
I'd been to The White House.

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:39.434
And I was very nervous.

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:43.734
And he came in and he took
my hand and he said,

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:46.100
"Welcome to this house."

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.901
And then he went,
"Welcome to this house."

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:51.968
And when he turned,
he was completely cross-eyed,

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.801
because his eyes
were very close.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:57.534
So it was,
"Welcome to this house."

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.267
Way too close.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:08.667
-I can't top that one.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:12.400
Okay. That's a good one.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.834
I went to The White House.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:16.968
I got invited to do stand-up,
open up for the Foo Fighters

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.300
on the Fourth of July, outside
on the East Lawn, for veterans.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.667
And I went there.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.801
And I went and I was so nervous
to meet the president.

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.200
It was Obama.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.267
Barack Obama and Michelle Obama.
And I got so nervous.

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.434
I said, "I'm going to bring
my best suit."

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:31.234
And my best suit --
it was a three-piece suit.

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:33.400
So I wore a three-piece suit.
It was the Fourth of July.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.100
Probably maybe 100, 105 degrees.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.534
-Yeah. Right. Exactly.

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:39.467
-And I'm getting there
and I am just sweating.

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:40.567
It is a disaster.

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:41.934
And I'm there,
and the Foo Fighters

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.667
get off their thing and
they're wearing board shorts.

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:46.033
And they're like, "Hey, Jimmy.
Man, you're hot."

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:47.234
And I go, "Yeah, man.

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:48.434
I'm ready to meet
the president, you know?"

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:49.934
I'm, like,
trying not to pass out.

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:53.100
And, so, I do my bit.
I'm just totally just drenched.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.701
And I -- Finally,
they make you wait on line

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:55.767
to go get your picture
taken with

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:56.868
the First Lady
and the president.

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:57.868
-Right.

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.167
-And I'm waiting on line
to go see

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.968
the president and the
First Lady, and I finally --

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:05.000
I finally get up to
the front of the thing,

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.334
and I'm just a disaster.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.300
And they both
start laughing at me.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.300
And Michelle Obama
loosens my tie,

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.467
and she's like,
"Oh, my God, you must be hot."

00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:14.234
And I go...

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:15.234
And then I'm just --
She said I looked like

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:16.400
I was gonna pass out.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.100
And I looked at the president
and I go --

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.267
He goes, "Jimmy,
didn't you get the memo?

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.501
It's a barbecue."

00:04:22.501 --> 00:04:24.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.133
Let's get to our final topic.

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:31.734
This last round
is worth 1,000 points.

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:32.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:35.601
[ Beeping ]

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.901
-[ Stutters ]

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:39.501
-Tom Hanks.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:41.634
Oh, can I tell -- I'll tell my
Tom Hanks story first?

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.267
-Yeah.

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:46.133
By the way,
it's pronounced "Tom Hank."

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:47.267
The "S" is silent.

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:48.934
Very few people about it.
Go ahead.

00:04:48.934 --> 00:04:50.634
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:54.534
Does that count as your story?

00:04:54.534 --> 00:04:56.267
-It should, but it won't.

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:58.400
-Tom Hanks was
nice enough to cast me in

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.634
"Band of Brothers,"
an amazing miniseries on HBO.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.434
-So he'd seen "Fever Pitch."

00:05:03.434 --> 00:05:06.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:08.467
-No. He'd not seen any of
my work up until that moment.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:09.767
-Oh, okay.

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:11.467
-And, so, we're doing this.
And it's World War II.

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:13.701
And it's a really amazing
miniseries, if you ever see it.

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:15.400
So, I'm in one of the episodes.
I have one line.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.234
I go like, "Good luck, boys."
You know?

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:19.067
And I have to pull up in a Jeep.
And I go, "Great."

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:20.734
And he goes, "Do you know how
to drive stick?"

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:21.934
I go, "I don't.

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:23.968
I don't know
how to drive automatic.

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:25.133
I'm terrible."

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:26.601
He's like, "Alright,
let's learn how to do it.

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:27.834
It's a World War II Jeep."
I go, "Okay."

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.067
So, you got to go in,

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.801
you got to put it
and make sure it's in neutral,

00:05:30.801 --> 00:05:33.767
push in the clutch, turn it on,
turn the thing,

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:36.934
start it up, put it in first,
get rid of the clutch

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:38.834
as you push the gas
and take off.

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.801
Again, I have one line, okay?

00:05:40.801 --> 00:05:42.367
So I go --
Okay, so, it took me like

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:43.634
an hour to do this thing,
you know?

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:44.801
And it's just awful.

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:46.300
It's just ruining the buzz
and everything.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.567
So I finally figured out how to
go and how to get going.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:49.701
And, so, I'm going.

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:51.634
And Tom is like,
"Okay, this is a disaster."

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:53.300
I go, "Just drive around,
figure it out."

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:54.801
He goes, "Because we're going to
wait for nightfall

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:55.901
for your scene."

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:58.400
I go,
"We're doing this at night?"

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.100
So now I've got to
turn headlights on, okay?

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.767
So, somehow, they figured it out
so the stunt double or

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:06.367
someone drives the Jeep down
and does my Jeep driving.

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:08.634
So, then I'm in the thing,
and I've got to do my lines.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.567
This is my camera.
I go, "Good luck, boys."

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:15.400
And then I go, "Click, on,
neutral, thing, clutch,

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:20.167
thing, headlights, on,
like, good luck."

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:22.667
And awful.
It couldn't be worse, right?

00:06:22.667 --> 00:06:24.734
So, then -- Wait.
So it's terrible.

00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:25.801
So they go, "Cut!"

00:06:25.801 --> 00:06:27.267
Tom's like,
"Everything okay, buddy?

00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:28.434
All good?"

00:06:28.434 --> 00:06:30.167
I go, "Yeah, I just don't know
how to drive --"

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:32.834
And there's 200 extras, and
soldiers were walking around.

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:33.934
And I go,
"I'm totally embarrassed."

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:35.434
He goes, "Here's what you do.

00:06:35.434 --> 00:06:36.968
Say your line, press the clutch,

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:40.601
and I'm going to have someone
push the Jeep

00:06:40.601 --> 00:06:41.734
out of the frame," okay?

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:42.801
So I go, "Okay, great."

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:44.434
So, I go there,
and I'm so nervous.

00:06:44.434 --> 00:06:46.334
You know, I'm nervous.
I'm gonna do the thing.

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:47.934
And I got, you know, fake dirt
on my face and all this stuff,

00:06:47.934 --> 00:06:49.100
and I'm wearing a hat.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.200
I'm a soldier.
And I go, "Good luck, boys."

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.200
And I forget to press
the clutch,

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.734
which means
the wheels won't move.

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:58.434
So there's two guys
pushing the Jeep.

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:01.400
Pushing the Jeep.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.734
And if you --
My face is going...

00:07:02.734 --> 00:07:04.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:08.667 --> 00:07:10.734
...out of the frame.

00:07:10.734 --> 00:07:11.734
-Oh, that's good.

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:13.300
-And if you watch
the miniseries,

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.968
they added Jeep sound effects.

00:07:14.968 --> 00:07:17.567
So, I go, "Good luck, boys,"
and you hear...

00:07:17.567 --> 00:07:19.701
[ Imitates engine revving ]

00:07:19.701 --> 00:07:21.667
Alright. And I've never
worked with him since.

00:07:21.667 --> 00:07:24.033
So, thank you. No.
That's my Tom Hanks story.

00:07:24.033 --> 00:07:26.033
-That's a good story.
-He was very nice.

00:07:26.033 --> 00:07:28.434
-That's a good story.

00:07:28.434 --> 00:07:29.634
-It's a decent story.

00:07:29.634 --> 00:07:33.868
-My story
is that Tom, Steve Martin,

00:07:33.868 --> 00:07:35.801
and our friend Walter Parkes
and I

00:07:35.801 --> 00:07:39.133
do a once-every-four-year
or -three-year

00:07:39.133 --> 00:07:41.801
colonoscopy party.

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:45.801
We go to Steve's house,

00:07:45.801 --> 00:07:50.200
and it's all set very formally
with, like, the barium.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:52.367
And then we toast each other.

00:07:52.367 --> 00:07:54.267
We call it "Colonoscopy Eve."

00:07:54.267 --> 00:07:56.467
It's the night before.
-Of course.

00:07:56.467 --> 00:08:00.167
-And we toast each other. And...
[ Gargling ]

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:02.234
And then Tom says,
"Why make that noise?

00:08:02.234 --> 00:08:03.367
Just drink it."

00:08:03.367 --> 00:08:08.133
And then, you know --
Then we play poker

00:08:08.133 --> 00:08:11.934
or, you know --
you know, there's some,

00:08:11.934 --> 00:08:13.601
you know, "Pam &amp; Tommy."

00:08:13.601 --> 00:08:15.434
You know, Steve's taped stuff
that we can watch.

00:08:15.434 --> 00:08:16.801
And...

00:08:16.801 --> 00:08:22.367
And then -- And here's --
And then we sleep all together.

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:24.067
They're, like, bunk beds,
like The Stooges -- one bed.

00:08:24.067 --> 00:08:25.534
And here's
the thing about Steve.

00:08:25.534 --> 00:08:27.834
You'd think, with his wealth,
he wouldn't have one bathroom.

00:08:27.834 --> 00:08:30.067
So, but he --
And so, by midnight,

00:08:30.067 --> 00:08:32.467
it looks like day 15
of a Carnival Cruise,

00:08:32.467 --> 00:08:34.801
you know, that bathroom.

00:08:34.801 --> 00:08:35.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:35.901 --> 00:08:37.334
-You are the greatest.

00:08:37.334 --> 00:08:38.501
Martin Short.
-Aw, come on.

00:08:38.501 --> 00:08:41.300
-He's the winner.
And you are a great storyteller.

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:44.033
I just wanted to trick you
into telling stories.

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:46.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:46.667 --> 00:08:48.100
-I love you.

00:08:52.033 --> 00:08:53.100
-Martin Short.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.901
"Only Murders in the Building,"

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:57.534
Season 2 finale airs
this Tuesday on Hulu.

00:08:57.534 --> 00:08:58.734
We're talking to Juno Temple
